#: ../../source/docs/common-antenna-tracking.rst:7
#: 3d337bd9e3d34284b8e06635f8378627
msgid "*Antenna Trackers* are systems that track your vehicle's location, and use this information to correctly align a directional antenna. This approach significantly improves the range over which signals can be both sent and received from the ground station."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-antenna-tracking.rst:10
#: 4d41c44be6a24df0bc769acd81c54ca5
msgid "ArduPilot supports two methods for Antenna Tracking. One method uses GPS information from the vehicle and ground station to aim the antenna. The other uses an autopilot board and gets its GPS directly via telemetry from the vehicle so this :ref:`AntennaTracker <antennatracker:home>` is independent of any particular GCS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-antenna-tracking.rst:13
#: 9d743fd910e6419eafdf9f91cc19d7ec
msgid ":ref:`ArduPilot Autopilot based AntennaTracker <antennatracker:home>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-antenna-tracking.rst:15
#: c7bed37b30914b6ead53105969724acb
msgid "The AntennaTracker firmware turns an ArduPilot-supported board (:ref:`common-autopilots`) nto the controller for an antenna tracker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-antenna-tracking.rst:16
#: d4a311bba1b04d2c80aacf97363b25c8
msgid "The board calculates the required antenna direction and can drive the antenna's servos directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-antenna-tracking.rst:17
#: 63ce618bc1a14f12803a664040af917a
msgid "Mission Planner (or any other GCS) may be used, but is not required."
msgstr ""

